        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: переносить",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "переносить (perenosít) — \"to postpone, to move (to another time); to carry over\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Мы переносим встречу на понедельник. My perenósim vstréchu na ponedélnik. We are moving the meeting to Monday."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperfective; present переношу, переносишь; perfective перенести. Переносить на + accusative — to move to. It also means to bear: плохо переносить (perenosít) холод."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "переносить (perenosít) is built from пере- \"across, over\" and носить \"to carry\", inherited from Proto-Slavic: to carry a meeting over to another day."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
